Dolphin network-library references

The ip/ sources and include/dolphin-network/ headers derive from Cuyler36's
public GameCube SocketLibrary reconstruction:
https://github.com/Cuyler36/dolsocketlibrary
Commit: e02356692695e64429dd70dc421a4a71a493e9c8

eth/md5.c derives from Cuyler36's public NetworkBasePackage reconstruction:
https://github.com/Cuyler36/dolnetbp
Commit: ba3846a83bf86505fe60e07aefe89e3e0ffc0e34

The MD5 implementation is the RSA Data Security, Inc. MD5 Message-Digest
Algorithm. Its complete copyright and permission notice is retained in md5.c.
Other source/header notices are preserved as supplied. Neither reference
repository supplies a repository-wide license; no broader license grant is
asserted here.

Only the manifest-listed, completely verified retained functions are accepted.
Unretained APIs and header facilities are not verified against this target.
AI assisted reference selection, integration and byte verification.
See docs/Network.md and config/GR8E69/dolphin-network-source.json.

Additional reference: bfbbdecomp/bfbb
https://github.com/bfbbdecomp/bfbb
Commit: 8fb1c232addcacf44932c10c4cede41b43f98f40

eth/base64.c, eth/ethsec.c and include/dolphin-ethernet/ derive from that
project's public Dolphin reconstruction. Its CC0 notice is preserved in
LICENSE.bfbb; the RSA Data Security, Inc. MD5 Message-Digest Algorithm header
retains its own copyright and permission notice. See the per-file provenance
records for modifications and original hashes. The imported Ethernet header
uses the existing os.h umbrella for OSTime instead of the narrower reference
include. Source integration adds required declarations and casts; ethsec omits
the later port-1900 exemptions absent from the target.

IPRoute restores the observed older broadcast-address rules. DHCPDump and
IPDnsDiagnostic are explicitly scoped source fragments, not recovered complete
historical files. DNS diagnostic types are limited to the original 17 entries.
Only complete manifest-listed functions and all emitted storage are accepted.
